    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Using a calculator, (i) the PMCC is r ≈0.7555 . [A1] (ii) The fitted line is ˆc = 2.8 + 1.1m . [M1] [A1] (b) Substitute expenditure in thousands of pounds: 2.8 + 1.1(8.8) = 2.8 + 9.68 and 2.8 + 1.1(20) = 2.8 + 22. At m = 8.8 the model estimates 12.48, or about 12 cars: [M1] This is interpolation in the observed range 6 ≤m ≤10. [A1] At m = 20 it estimates 24.8, or about 25 cars: [A1] This is far beyond the sample range and is unreliable: [A1] (c) The model predicts 2.8 sales in a month with zero expenditure, which is outside the sample range: [B1] Each extra £1000 in monthly expenditure is associated with an increase of 1.1 in predicted sales: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
