    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The events A and B satisfy P A ( ) = x ,        ( ) P B = y ,        ( A ∪ B ) = ,            ( B A = ) P 0.6 P 0.2 . a) Show clearly that x + y = ( ) 4 5 3 . 5 The events B and C are mutually exclusive such that P ( B ∪ C ) = 0.9 ,         ( ) P C = x + y . b) Find the value of x and the value of y . ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:568.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q7-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) Determine, showing all the relevant workings, whether the events A and B are statistically independent. ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:582.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The intersection has probability 0.2x. [B1] [A1] Hence x + y −0.2x = 0.6, [M1] [A1] so 4x + 5y = 3 . [A1] (b) Since B, C are mutually exclusive, y + (x + y) = 0.9. [B1] Eliminate x by multiplying x + 2y = 0.9 by four: Subtract 4x + 5y = 3 to obtain 3y = 0.6, then x = 0.9 −2(0.2). Solving x + 2y = 0.9 [M1] and 4x + 5y = 3 [A1] gives x = 0.5, y = 0.2 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(c) Alternatively P(A ∩B) = 0.2x = 0.1 equals P(A) P(B) = (0.5)(0.2). Since P(B | A) = 0.2 = P(B), the events are independent: [B1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:472.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The events A and B satisfy P A ( ) = x ,        ( ) P B = y ,        ( A ∪ B ) = ,            ( B A = ) P 0.6 P 0.2 . a) Show clearly that x + y = ( ) 4 5 3 . 5 The events B and C are mutually exclusive such that P ( B ∪ C ) = 0.9 ,         ( ) P C = x + y . b) Find the value of x and the value of y . ( ) 4 c) Determine, showing all the relevant workings, whether the events A and B are statistically independent. ( ) 2"
