    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-r/q8",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A B F 4 kg 30 N 6 kg Two blocks A and B of respective masses 4 kg and 6 kg lie on a smooth horizontal surface and are connected by a light inextensible string. Two collinear forces, of magnitudes F N and 30 N , act on each of the blocks, and in opposite directions, as shown in the figure above.\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q8-question-2.svg\" alt=\"ms−. 2 The system has constant acceleration of magnitude 2 Determine the possible values of F , and in each case the corresponding value of the tension in the string. ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:585.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Taking rightwards as positive, the whole system gives 30 −F = 10a. [M1] [A1] For block B, 30 −T = 6a. [M1] [A1] For the first block alone T −F = 4a. If a = 2, then T = 30 −12 = 18, F = 18 −8 = 10. If a = −2, then T = 30 + 12 = 42, F = 42 + 8 = 50.\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Thus a (m s−2) F (N) T (N) +2 10 18 [M1] [A1] −2 50 42 Both tensions are positive, so both cases are possible . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 8 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
