    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-r/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"− 1 v ( ms ) 16 t ( )s 0 5 The figure above shows the speed time graph ( ,t v of a particle in a straight line ) between two points, A and B .\" style=\"--madas-width:566.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"ms− and constant 1 At t = 0 , the particle is observed passing through A with speed 16 ms−, which it maintains until 2 acceleration of 1.6 t = 5 . For t ≥ 5 , the particle moves with constant speed which it maintains until it is 820 m from A . As soon the particle is reaches a distance of 820 m from A , it decelerates uniformly ms−, coming to rest at B . 2 at 4 Determine in any order the distance AB and the total time taken for the particle to travel from A to B . ( ) 10\" style=\"--madas-width:596.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The first phase ends at speed 16 + 1.6(5) = 24 m s−1 [M1] after a distance 1 2(16 + 24)(5) = 100 m. [A1] The constant speed section is 820 −100 = 720 m [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-r/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"and takes 720/24 = 30 s. [M1] Braking takes 24/4 = 6 s [M1] and covers 1 2(24)(6) = 72 m. [A1] Add the three times 5 + 30 + 6. The total distance is the sum 100 + 720 + 72, or the known 820 metres before braking plus the braking triangle. Hence AB = 892 m [M1] [A1] and the journey takes 41 s . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
